const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文提出保留时间序列依赖结构的 stationary bootstrap 重采样方法。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"The paper proposes stationary-bootstrap resampling to preserve dependence in time series. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"方法通过随机区块长度和连续观测片段构造重采样序列，设计选择决定其保留的依赖特征。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It constructs resampled series from random block lengths and contiguous observations; those choices determine which dependence features survive. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"输入是按固定时钟排序的完整时间序列、缺失处理规则、抽样区块设置和统计量定义。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"Inputs are a complete, fixed-clock time series, missing-data treatment, block settings, and a defined statistic. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"它提供对时间依赖数据进行不确定性评估的一种工具，而不是使任何小样本或非平稳数据自动可靠。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"It is a tool for uncertainty assessment with dependent data, not a device that makes any small or nonstationary sample reliable. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not convert association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"记录频率、缺失段和区块长度设定，检验重采样是否尊重交易时段和结构断点，并保存随机种子。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Record frequency, missing segments, block-length setting, trading-session and structural-break treatment, and random seed. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994)。重采样假设无法替代对非平稳、制度变化或样本选择的诊断，更不证明预测或策略有效。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994). The resampling assumption does not replace diagnosis of nonstationarity, institutional change, or selection, and proves neither a forecast nor a strategy. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1994.10476870",label:{zh:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of the American Statistical Association (1994) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“The Stationary Bootstrap”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。重采样假设无法替代对非平稳、制度变化或样本选择的诊断，更不证明预测或策略有效。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “The Stationary Bootstrap”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
